<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16947" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτάλλω</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ],
			</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀταλός</span>) only in
		pres. and impf., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>skip in childish glee, gambol,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄταλλε δὲ κήτε᾽ ὑπ᾽ αὐτοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.27
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Mosch.
				2.116
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				2.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>bring up a child, rear, foster,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
				<u>Epigr.</u>
				4.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέαν ψυχὴν ἀτάλλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					559
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλπὶς ἀτάλλοισα καρδίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					214
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>grow up, wax,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Merc.
				400
			</span></i>:—
				Act.
			, intr. in this sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτρέφετ᾽
				ἀτάλλων [ᾱτ</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				131
			</span></i>.—Poet. and later Prose.</div>
